  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 211 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nAn upper level high is expected to track across the northern Plains, \nwhile the southern jet stream remains well south of the region. This \npattern will bring us more towards seasonal high temperatures \nThursday into the weekend, with mostly dry conditions expected. With \nthe upper high remaining across the northern Plains, expecting that \nthe upper level trough forecast for this weekend will continue to \nremain well north of the region. Latest guidance continues to show \nthis trend, and with this northern trend, expecting little to no \nprecipitation this weekend. Even latest ensemble guidance is now \npicking up on this northern trend, keeping a less than 10 percent \nchance for measureable precipitation this weekend. As for \ntemperatures, expecting that highs will mostly remain in the 50s \nthis week, with slightly warming highs to the upper 50s and possibly \nlower 60s by this weekend. This is around normal for this time of \nyear, as typical highs for early November are around 55 to 58 \ndegrees. \n\nBy early next week, slight upper level ridging is expected to build \nacross the northern Plains. This may lead to subtle temperature \nincreases, with the current forecast bringing highs into the low to \nmid 60s. This would push highs around 5 to 10 degrees above normal. \nHowever, will continue to keep an eye on the forecast trends this \nweek, as guidance comes into better consensus resolving the upper \nlevel pattern after this weekend.",
